I’ll give you a quick update on Stream 4, the MyIAM AI Agent project.

Most of you are probably already familiar with MyIAM, whether it's for requesting access, tracking a request, or managing access for your teams.

Today, even for relatively simple needs, users sometimes have to spend time figuring out where to find the right information, which procedure to follow, or where to go to perform a specific action.

**And that's exactly why we launched the MyIAM AI Agent.**

Our objective is to build an AI chatbot for all MyIAM end users, leveraging both Generative and Agentic AI capabilities, to provide a single entry point to IAM information and services, making them easier and more intuitive for users to access.

**To deliver this, the project relies on two core capabilities.**

The first is **RAG**, which enables the Agent to answer users' questions instantly based on our IAM Knowledge Base.

The second is **Agentic AI**, which connects directly to MyIAM data via APIs, pulling user-specific, real-time data to answer context-aware questions.
